
- Read PROJECT_BRIEF.md first. Items marked TO CONFIRM are unknown ask me, do not guess.
- If something is unverified (reciter identity, text-to-audio word mapping, formant accuracy), say so in your output.
- Never invent results, file contents, or library behavior. If a command fails, show the error and stop.

## Safety
- Never modify or delete anything in data/. Write outputs only to results/ and scripts/.
- Ask before installing packages, downloading large files, or running anything over ~5 minutes.
- Before editing an existing file, tell me which file and why.

## Method
- Python only (plus Praat via parselmouth if needed). Fixed random seeds. Scripts must be re-runnable.
- Always split train/test by surah (GroupKFold), never randomly by clip, word, or vowel.
- Always report a majority baseline and a duration-only baseline next to any model.
- Compare the same word (same SURAH_AYAH_WORD) across styles. Derive style from the folder name.
- Log every excluded item with a reason and a count.

## Framing
- Descriptive phonetics only. Do not rank styles or reciters or make religious judgments.

## Working style
- Work one phase at a time. At the end of each phase, write a short summary to results/phase_N.md
  (what was done, numbers, problems, open questions) and stop.
- Prefer small scripts with clear names (01_data_audit.py, 02_text_mapping.py, ...).